                {
                    "file": "lib/rest_client.robot",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "# Authenticate to OpenBMC/Redfish in a backward\u2011compatible way:\n    # 1) Try *Legacy Redfish* `/login` and, on success,\n    #    initialize session object \"openbmc\".\n    # 2) If that fails, try *Redfish SessionService*\n    #    `/redfish/v1/SessionService/Sessions`\n    #    and, on success, initialize session object \"redfish\".\n    # 3) Else, try *Legacy REST* `/login` and, on success,\n    #    initialize session object \"openbmc\".\n\n    # Legacy BMC web /login\n    ${bmcweb_status}=  Run Keyword And Return Status\n    ...  BMC Web Login Request  ${timeout}  ${rest_username}  ${rest_password}\n    IF  ${bmcweb_status} == ${True}  RETURN\n\n    # Redfish SessionService login\n    ${redfish_status}=  Run Keyword And Return Status\n    ...  Redfish Login  ${timeout}  ${rest_username}  ${rest_password}\n    IF  ${redfish_status} == ${True}  RETURN"
                },
                {
                    "file": "lib/rest_client.robot",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "It doesn\u2019t change the preference that you are adding. The intention is simply to ensure that systems with different combinations of legacy and newer authentication implementations have a fair chance to detect and initialize the correct session type.\n\nLegacy REST and older Redfish\u2011legacy implementations that use /login initialize the session object named \"openbmc\", whereas the Redfish SessionService initializes the session object named \"redfish\".\nPrabha, please make the above changes.\n\nThis behavior exists due to historical evolution of the authentication flow. We have not yet fully removed the older implementation, but it is being deprecated gradually as we move toward standard Redfish SessionService.\nPlease take care of this update."
                },
                {
                    "file": "lib/rest_client.robot",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prabha Veerubhotla",
                        "email": "vvlprabha@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Prabha-Veerubhotla"
                    },
                    "message": "That makes sense. Thanks for pointing this out."
                },
                {
                    "file": "lib/rest_client.robot",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prabha Veerubhotla",
                        "email": "vvlprabha@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Prabha-Veerubhotla"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
